#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsChangelogAbilitiesRegistrar.php:26
msgid "Get Changelog"
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsChangelogAbilitiesRegistrar.php:27
msgid ""
"Retrieve the IvyForms changelog, including latest version updates, features, improvements, \n"
"                and bug fixes.\n"
"\n"
"                Use this ability ONLY when the user explicitly asks for:\n"
"                - changelog\n"
"                - release notes\n"
"                - what changed in IvyForms\n"
"                - version updates or update history\n"
"\n"
"                Do NOT use this ability for:\n"
"                - plugin settings\n"
"                - documentation\n"
"                - feature explanation unrelated to versions\n"
"                - support/debugging issues\n"
"\n"
"                This is a READ-ONLY informational endpoint and does not modify any data."
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:30
msgid "List Entries"
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:31
msgid ""
"List IvyForms form entries (submissions) with pagination, optional text search, form filter, and sorting. Through this MCP ability, orderBy is limited to id or formName \n"
"                (matching the plugin list UI)."
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:108
msgid "Get Entry"
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:109
msgid ""
"Retrieve a single IvyForms form entry (submission) by entryId.\n"
"\n"
"                Returns the entry record plus field values suitable for inspecting one submission.\n"
"\n"
"                Use this ability when the user asks to:\n"
"                - open or view details for one entry when its ID is known\n"
"                - inspect field values submitted in a single response\n"
"\n"
"                DO NOT use this ability when the user wants:\n"
"                - multiple entries or a list/browse flow → use ivyforms/list-entries\n"
"                - form structure or builder fields → use ivyforms/get-form\n"
"                - notifications or emails → use notification abilities\n"
"\n"
"                Entry content/status editing is not exposed as an MCP ability; only starring is available\n"
"                 via ivyforms/update-entry-starred.\n"
"\n"
"                This is READ-ONLY. The response includes adminLink when the entry resolves successfully."
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:141
#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:274
#: backend/src/Services/Translations/BackendStrings.php:1475
msgid "Invalid entry ID."
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:179
msgid "Get Entry Count"
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:180
msgid ""
"Retrieve the total number of IvyForms entries (submissions) for one or more form IDs.\n"
"\n"
"                This ability returns ONLY counts (aggregated numbers), not entry data.\n"
"\n"
"                Use this ability when the user asks:\n"
"                - how many entries a form has\n"
"                - total submissions count\n"
"                - number of responses for one or more forms\n"
"                - entry statistics in the form of counts only\n"
"\n"
"                DO NOT use this ability for:\n"
"                - listing actual entries → use ivyforms/list-entries\n"
"                - retrieving a single entry → use ivyforms/get-entry\n"
"                - searching or filtering entry data → use ivyforms/list-entries\n"
"                - analytics or reporting beyond simple totals\n"
"\n"
"                This is a READ-ONLY aggregation endpoint and does not return individual entry records.\n"
"\n"
"                Provide formIds as an array; the response includes counts keyed by each form ID."
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:242
msgid "Update Entry Starred"
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsEntriesAbilitiesRegistrar.php:243
msgid ""
"Mark an IvyForms entry as starred or unstarred (favorite toggle).\n"
"                This ability updates ONLY the \"starred\" status of an entry and does NOT modify entry content.\n"
"\n"
"                Use this ability when the user wants to:\n"
"                - star an entry\n"
"                - mark an entry as important or favorite\n"
"                - unstar or remove star from an entry\n"
"                - toggle entry priority or bookmarking state\n"
"\n"
"                DO NOT use this ability for:\n"
"                - editing entry field values or read/unread status (not exposed as an MCP ability)\n"
"                - listing or viewing entries → use list-entries or get-entry\n"
"                - bulk updates or modifications beyond star status\n"
"\n"
"                This is a SAFE STATE CHANGE operation that only toggles a single boolean flag (starred/unstarred)."
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsFieldsAbilitiesRegistrar.php:31
msgid "Add Form Field"
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsFieldsAbilitiesRegistrar.php:32
msgid "Add a new field to an existing IvyForms form. Supported types: text, textarea, email, number, phone, website, name, radio, checkbox, select, multi-select, address, date, time, rating, html, slider, file-upload, gdpr, product, quantity, total. When IvyForms Pro is active, password, signature, date_time, likert, nps, and rich_text are also supported. After adding a field, use open-form-builder to let the user see and configure. For multipage forms (Pro), pass pageId (e.g. page_1) to place the field on a specific page."
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsFieldsAbilitiesRegistrar.php:141
msgid "Add Form Fields"
msgstr ""

#: backend/src/Infrastructure/WP/MCP/Abilities/IvyFormsFieldsAbilitiesRegistrar.php:142
msgid ""
"Add one or more new fields to an existing IvyForms form. This ability modifies stored form configuration \n"
"                (writes the whole form payload like the builder save). REQUIRED INPUTS: formId and fields (each item requires type). \n"
"                Optional per-field keys mirror add-form-field. SUPPORTED FIELD TYPES: text, textarea, email, number, phone, website, name, radio, checkbox, select, multi-select, address, date, time, rating, html, slider, file-upload, gdpr, product, quantity, total. If IvyForms Pro is active, password, signature, date_time, likert, nps, and rich_text fields are also supported. IMPORTANT WORKFLOW RULES: 1. This ability ONLY adds fields to an existing form (it does NOT create a form). 2. If formId is missing or unknown, the agent MUST first use get-forms or \n"
"                create-form before calling this. 3. After successfully adding fields, the next step should usually be open-form-builder\n"
"                 so the user can review layout and options. 4. Do not assume field ordering unless explicitly returned by the API response. FIELD BEHAVIOR NOTES: - label defaults to a capitalized version of type if not provided. - required defaults to false. - width defaults to 100 if not specified. - description is helper text shown under the field in UI. COMMON AGENT MISTAKES TO AVOID: - Do NOT call this if the user wants to create a form (use create-form instead). - Do NOT assume the field already exists after calling this ability until API confirms success. - Do NOT duplicate fields manually; use duplicate-form-field for that purpose."
msgstr ""

